    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;be the circumcentre of the triangle formed by the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>69</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>61</mn></math>. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
