  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;be the circumcentre of the triangle formed by the lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>69</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>61</mn></math>,</p><p>Now plotting the diagram of the above equations and finding the intersection point we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cba25b99-b4ba-4bbd-b387-c472417d4013.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>Now from diagram we can see that it is a right-angled triangle, so the circumcentre is given by midpoint of the hypotenuse,</p><p>Hence, circumcentre will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
